And this is one of those cases where two a's meet each other and they became a long a (ā).

00:18:02.580 --> 00:18:09.420
But you don't know if 
the two a's that met each other were short a's or long a's, and it's very important with Prāṇāyāma

00:18:09.720 --> 00:18:16.160
to know that the first a was short 
and the second a was a long a (ā).

00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:25.020
So, a + yama would mean "not to control the breath". 
And ā + yama would mean "perfect control of the breath",  to where you could actually hold it.

00:18:25.140 --> 00:18:26.560
And that's called @SBYOR.

00:18:26.560 --> 00:18:33.120
So one of the words for breathing practice in tibetan is @RLUNG SBYOR and it's here.

